      "details": "The boot-config buffer is freed if allocated, including when its read helper returns an error after allocation. The flash-access allocation is checked in the same cleanup after every initialized path. Each free is conditional on syna_request_managed_device() returning non-NULL; if it returns NULL, the devm allocation remains tied to device teardown instead of being released immediately. Ghidra stock has the same two lookups and conditional frees. Static evidence did not establish that the provider becomes unavailable between allocation and cleanup, so this is a conditional retained-devres risk, not a confirmed runtime leak.",
